model {
  extend basalt {
    build = module "Build" {
      description "The pool Worker typecheck uses only platform declarations. Shared fetch telemetry preserves browser-only options when present, and redirect policy serializes URL bases before platform parsing. Pull requests always run source checks and select heavy jobs from changed repository paths and both sides of each changed carry. Unknown inputs and shared infrastructure select every job. The aggregate accepts skips only for unselected jobs and requires successful fast checks and selected jobs. Main and release updates retain the complete suite. Public source exports support the fast typecheck; production builds independently check shipped declarations and Worker startup limits. Existing runner configuration only routes selected suites to hosted jobs or Boat bundles. The aggregate requires the selected route to finish successfully; unrelated changes start no bundle. The focused app-listener proof uses native HTTP because Node fetch replaces an explicit Host header. The backend must observe the exact requested app host through the held origin. Each production-operation binding proof runs alone with its own database. The scope runner builds the shared framework once after installing its proof inputs, and each isolated managed run explicitly reuses that unchanged build output. The hosted fallback assigns each identity scenario its own matrix job. Boat bundles retain a private prepared tree per suite because signed proof runners modify source in place. CI assigns each identity scenario its own matrix job so independent Cloud startup costs do not accumulate against one job deadline. A reviewed flake list names each temporary exception and its owning fix. Only final reports with explicit zero unhandled and suite errors can classify a known failure. Physical checks require an accounts-only checksum diff at the unchanged comparison; fixture removal requires a passed body before its exact teardown failure. Missing evidence and every other failure remain blocking. Removing an entry restores blocking without changing the test. Before Vitest starts, binding variants preboot original and changed Alchemy stages with the same canonical origin and configured secrets; timed fixture operations only switch the retained listener, and suite teardown owns both runtimes. App lint reads the immutable host manifest from the exact pinned Git object in its sparse source checkout and then applies manifest carries. It needs no live content API request or host installation. The shared-account health scenario runs in the hosted account gate and identifies status dots by their image role. Physical database fixtures hold runner-owned shared table locks across the clone and both account and receipt baseline reads. Physical database fixtures wait for completed initial user setup and saved default-account links before cloning. PostgreSQL commit notifications wake a fresh readiness read; unrelated member work does not delay the baseline. Runner-owned shared table locks cover the clone and both account and receipt baseline reads. The lock scope rolls back before target selection and releases on failure, so normal writes resume after the consistent baseline is captured. Managed Cloud owns retained canonical API and app loopback listeners before creating fixtures. Alchemy binds their private listeners on OS-assigned ports with bind-only collision recovery; each resource's own successful startup announcement supplies its forwarding destination. Original and changed preboot runtimes own distinct app origins. Deliberate restarts keep each canonical origin and replace only its destination. Managed Cloud owns a retained canonical loopback listener before creating fixtures. The production-operation database proxy also binds an OS-assigned loopback listener before allocating its backend and keeps it for the environment scope. Runtime bindings and fixture replies use that actual held port. Proxy startup and cleanup failures retain only closed OS codes and bounded errno values; raw exception messages and nested causes never enter diagnostics. Alchemy binds the private API on an OS-assigned port with bind-only collision recovery, and startup output supplies the actual forwarding destination. Deliberate restarts keep the canonical origin and replace only that destination. Managed Cloud startup retains sanitized Alchemy failure output through stream completion or a bounded quiet period before rejecting readiness. The same cause reaches cloud.log and the startup error; successful readiness has no extra wait. Compiler evidence waits on saved-line notifications through authenticated fixture control until its trace and source digest reach the requested phase, within the scenario's existing deadline. Documentation builds read licensed Latin Geist faces from repository assets through the local font provider, including normal and italic variable weight ranges. CI rebuilds with empty font caches and refuses font requests to the outside service. Live model-probe capture keeps bounded response bodies, including non-JSON failures, with credentials redacted before evidence leaves the browser. The dashboard renderer excludes browser analytics through the framework compiler's client-only boundary; browser event capture and replay keep the same synchronous entry points. The final pool image declares its OAuth completion-receipt capability so upgrading that runtime changes the published image fingerprint. Worker builds place hashed chunks below a chunks directory, leaving exactly one root entry for startup profiling regardless of hash characters. Container reconciliation checks the observed image against the retained publication digest even when input hashes match. Each production release verifies the published manifest and config bytes against their digests, reads the actual platform and OAuth completion capability label, and captures that evidence with its candidate and input fingerprint. It then verifies the application and every active instance before recording success. Missing publication evidence, failed readiness or drift stops without automatic rollback."
      metadata { code "scripts|.upstream/e2e|assets/fonts/geist|e2e/slack/catalog.mjs|e2e/slack/run.ts|e2e/aws|containers/pool/fetch_releases.py|containers/pool/fetch_sources.py|containers/pool/Dockerfile|.github/workflows/ci.yml|.github/workflows/app-lint.yml|.github/workflows/client-desktop-mac.yml"; endpointHosts "127.0.0.1|localhost"; libraries "@modelcontextprotocol/sdk|node:http|@effect/platform-node|alchemy|esbuild|fontTools.subset|fontTools.ttLib.TTFont|yaml"; bindings "platform.env.POOL_OPERATIONS=basalt.modelGateway" }
    }
  }
}
